[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3222847239","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109944#issuecomment-3222847239","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109944","id":3222847239,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7AGL8H","user":{"login":"DanielKinsman","id":15639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman","html_url":"https://github.com/DanielKinsman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-26T06:47:45Z","updated_at":"2025-08-26T06:47:45Z","body":"I did look at fixing it further up the call stack but it seemed to be in generic importer land and not in anything blender related, and I didn't want to accidentally cause explosions for other well behaved importers.\r\n\r\n> Should headless mode perform autodetection? I believe it currently will return true without having set a path, which is inconsistent with the non-headless behavior which disables blend import and returns false.\r\n\r\nI don't know what \"autodetection\" is in this context? Disabling blend import seems to require saving and overwriting the user's editor settings which I am hesitant to do in a headless run. So I am avoiding that but returning `true` the same way that the [gui version does](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/modules/gltf/editor/editor_scene_importer_blend.cpp#L611) after it disables blend import. I must admit though, I don't know what the return value is supposed to signify, it doesn't appear to be documented. Testing it with both true and false, I get this behaviour:\r\n\r\n`true`: fails to import then segfaults.\r\n`false`: fails to import then the process exists with success (0 return code).\r\n\r\nI guess we probably want the second one, and people can inspect the output to determine success or failure? A non-zero return code would sure be ideal, but I guess that is a whole separate issue...\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3222847239/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314398994","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109944#issuecomment-3314398994","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109944","id":3314398994,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FjbcS","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"http